(findings . ((fail-closed-pinning . "tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt (27/27 green at implementation-sha) pins: the required-check set equals scripts/required-pr-checks.policy contents exactly (policy read as a Racket datum, file unmodified on the branch — git diff vs origin/main is empty); lint, security, release-dry-run, smoke (ubuntu-latest), test (0..2), test-aggregate, test-platform, workflows (0/1), workflows-aggregate are all required; fast-env plus prepared-env-report, shard-plan-report, and release-readiness are asserted NOT required; every aggregate job needs exactly its shard jobs; and the gate verdict function fails closed — each of the twelve required checks is individually removed in a test and the gate must return a named failure, never pass")
             (second-layer-pinning . "tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt re-pins the same graph as literal data at the integration layer (exit 0 at implementation-sha): the twelve-context list, aggregate needs edges (test-aggregate <- test (0..2) + test-platform; workflows-aggregate <- workflows (0), workflows (1)), and the fail-closed verdict semantics, so drift breaks two independent files")
             (snapshot-binding . "artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w0/graph-snapshot.json holds the live graph (branch-protection required contexts fetched via gh api, ci.yml needs-graph, non_required list) plus the same-SHA DAG timing baseline from PR #9606's run (head_sha c6ee39e4, per-job start/end for all 19 jobs); SHA256SUMS verifies clean (sha256sum -c OK) and the test asserts the snapshot checksum 6e0eee763b696c772482e3f4c3c060d95d96546c690394b2aa5f85139eb41a25 and the policy-equality comparison, so topology drift after W0 fails with a message naming both the pinned policy list and the snapshot list")
             (timing-baseline-scope . "the baseline is honestly one PR run at one point in time — documentation-grade shape reference for W1–W3, explicitly not a cohort; the evidence record carries the same honesty label")
             (delivery-scope . "the record correctly reserves the PR #9607 squash-merge and its merge SHA to the runtime coordinator's owned flow and does not claim them; the characterization deliberately gates itself with the same required-check graph it pins — the wave lands through the gate it characterizes")
             (attempt-history . "attempt-1's provider/network infra stop is recorded honestly; its committed work (27 characterization tests, snapshot, checksums) was resumed and extended, not redone; the evidence file was the only untracked residue and is now committed")))
(concerns . ((snapshot-freshness . "the snapshot is a point-in-time capture (2026-09-06T19:11:22Z); later waves intentionally re-snapshot and compare against this checksummed baseline — drift is a feature of the design, surfaced as a named failure, not a review concern")))
